Let a pushline consumer skip the cell conversion it does not read

sb_pushline_from_row() converts every cell of the departing row with
vterm_screen_get_cell() before handing the row to sb_pushline or
sb_pushline4. That is the right default -- the callback is told what
scrolled away -- and it is a full pass over the row for a consumer that
already keeps its own copy of the grid and takes the departing line from
that copy instead.

Such a consumer pays it on every line of output once the screen is full.
Measured with callgrind on 20,000 lines of plain text through a 200x50
grid: the conversion was 12.6% of the whole run, for cells the callback
never looked at.

Add vterm_screen_callbacks_pushline_without_cells(), an opt-in in the
shape of vterm_screen_callbacks_has_pushline4(). With it set the row is
not converted and the callbacks receive NULL for cells. NULL rather than
the untouched sb_buffer, so that a callback which reads anyway faults at
once instead of quietly copying whichever row was converted last.

Without the opt-in nothing changes.

